From: pdx203 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: bridge: metal2vulkan patch 0031, the rotated framebuffer over a portrait panel

Carries bridge/patches/0031-rotated-framebuffer-rows-on-ios.patch, which UniXNU's build-adreno-metal-bridge.py applies after
0030: on iOS a rotated texture skips the macOS-measured pitch rule (covers_its_row). QuartzCore draws landscape into a rotation-3
framebuffer-only texture of the landscape extent over the portrait panel's IOSurface, whose rows hold the portrait width; the rule
refused it ("Failed to allocate [2560 x 1096] BGRA framebuffer") and landscape froze on stale frames.

diff --git a/bridge/patches/0031-rotated-framebuffer-rows-on-ios.patch b/bridge/patches/0031-rotated-framebuffer-rows-on-ios.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/bridge/patches/0031-rotated-framebuffer-rows-on-ios.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+diff --git a/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/buffer_texture.rs b/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/buffer_texture.rs
+--- a/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/buffer_texture.rs
++++ b/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/buffer_texture.rs
+@@ -758,7 +758,15 @@
+     if !measured {
+         return Err(Error::NotImplemented(RuntimeGap::RotatedTexture));
+     }
+-    covers_its_row(texture).map_err(|problem| refusal_error(call, problem.into()))?;
++    // On iOS the pitch rule is macOS's alone: QuartzCore's landscape framebuffer on a portrait
++    // panel is a rotation-3 framebuffer-only texture of the landscape extent over the panel's
++    // portrait IOSurface, whose rows hold the portrait width (`CA::OGL::MetalContext::get_surface`,
++    // every iPad in landscape). Its passes render through the stored frame's rows (`turned`,
++    // the plane's own pitch); only its CPU access and blits, which a framebuffer-only texture has
++    // none of, address the plane at the texture's own wider rows.
++    if !cfg!(target_os = "ios") {
++        covers_its_row(texture).map_err(|problem| refusal_error(call, problem.into()))?;
++    }
+     let [width, height, depth] = texture.layout.extent;
+     let [width, height] = rotated::stored_extent(rotation, [width, height]);
+     let stored = BufferTexture {
